{
 "section_summary": "The section opens with a May 1944 embassy despatch enclosing intercepted commercial messages from April 10–18. The messages cover trade, shipping, finance, insurance, industrial equipment, and commodity controls across Japanese-occupied Asia. A June FBI memorandum then describes economic conditions in occupied North China and Japan, followed by a February State Department critique of proposals for Japan’s postwar economic rehabilitation.",
